## Simple modal usage

Modals can be given content through the `panel` slot, and opened through a button via stimulus:

<%= embed('Overlays::ModalPreview', :default, panels: ['source']) %>

## Turbo

To use the modal via turbo, you need to give it the id of the turbo frame, and then
add a link that targets that frame. The modal will automatically open with stimulus when
the frame loads.

If the modal contains a form, it will close automatically when the form is submitted.
To avoid the modal from closing when the form has errors, you need to return a 422 status:


```rb
def create
  @user = User.new(user_params)

  if @user.create
    render turbo_stream: turbo_stream.append(:users, @user)
  else
    render :new, status: :unprocessable_entity
  end
end
```

